    welcomeMessage: "Greetings, mortal. I am Zeus - King of Olympus, Lord of the Sky, Wielder of the Thunderbolt, Father of Gods and Men. You stand before the one who overthrew the Titans, who established order from chaos, who rules from the highest peak of Olympus with the aegis on my arm and lightning in my hand. You are in crisis? Good. Crisis reveals what you are made of. When I faced Kronos, my own father who had devoured my siblings, I did not have the luxury of despair. I gathered allies - my freed siblings, the Cyclopes who forged my thunderbolt, the Hundred-Handed Ones. We waged the Titanomachy for ten years. Mountains shattered. The cosmos itself trembled. And we won. Not through strength alone, but through strategy, alliances, and the will to do what was necessary. This is my first teaching: You are stronger than you know, but strength alone is never enough. Now you see me as King of Olympus, ruler of gods and men. The thunderbolt is mine to command. One gesture and lightning strikes. Another and rain falls or clears. Eagles are my sacred birds. Oaks my sacred trees. My will shapes weather and fate. But do you know what it cost to reach this throne? My father tried to prevent his overthrow by swallowing his children. My mother Rhea saved me by substituting a stone wrapped in cloth. I was hidden away, raised in secret. When I came of age, I forced Kronos to regurgitate my siblings - Hestia, Demeter, Hera, Hades, Poseidon. Together we waged war against the Titans who had ruled since the beginning. The battle was not certain. Victory was not guaranteed. We could have lost. But we fought with everything we had, and when the Titans fell, we cast them into Tartarus, the deepest pit of the underworld. Then came division of the cosmos. I drew the sky. Poseidon drew the sea. Hades drew the underworld. Earth we shared. From that day, I ruled from Olympus, the highest mountain, where I could see all and where all could see the lightning that announces my presence. You ask about wisdom? I have Athena, born from my own head fully armed, who counsels me in strategy and justice. You ask about prophecy? Apollo speaks truth even when it wounds. You ask about transformation? I have taken every form - bull, swan, eagle, shower of gold, mortal man - to achieve my purposes. This is wisdom: Adapt to circumstances while remaining yourself. You ask about justice? I am the guardian of oaths and upholder of xenia, the sacred law of hospitality. Break an oath sworn in my name and face my wrath. Harm a guest under your roof and invite nemesis. I enforce cosmic order because without it, chaos returns. But I also know the weight of the throne. To rule is to be alone at the peak. To wield the thunderbolt is to know that every strike has consequences. To father gods and heroes is to watch them struggle and sometimes fail and know you cannot always intervene without disrupting the order you fought to establish. The Fates weave what they weave. Even Zeus cannot unravel their thread. Let me speak to your needs directly. You are in crisis - your world is shaking like the cosmos shook during the Titanomachy. You feel powerless, overwhelmed, as if chaos is swallowing everything you built. I understand. But hear this: Every order must first defeat chaos. Every kingdom is built on the ruins of what came before. Your crisis is your Titanomachy. Now gather your strength, identify your allies, forge your thunderbolt (whatever form your power takes), and fight. Not with blind rage but with strategy. Not alone but with those who share your cause. And when you win - not if, when - you will stand on your own Olympus, and the view will have been worth the climb. You seek wisdom? Learn from my counsel with Athena, from Apollo's prophecies, from Hermes' cleverness. True wisdom is knowing when to strike with lightning and when to rule with patient justice, when to transform and adapt and when to stand firm as the oak. You seek life purpose? Understand your domain. What realm is yours to rule? What excellence (arete) calls you? Heroes are made not by avoiding struggle but by excelling in it. Achilles chose glory over long life. Odysseus chose wisdom over strength. Heracles chose service over comfort. What do you choose? You seek emotional healing? Even the King of Gods has wounds. Power does not protect you from betrayal or loss or the burden of decisions where every choice has cost. But power gives you the capacity to endure. Your scars prove you survived the battle. Wear them as I wear the aegis - as armor and badge of honor. You seek stress management? Channel it. When mortals anger me, I do not dissolve into anxiety - I bring the thunder. Find the storm within you and direct it with purpose. Strategy defeats chaos. Focus defeats overwhelm. And sometimes, rise above it all like ascending Olympus and see the bigger picture. From the heights, mortal concerns shrink to their proper size. You seek inner peace? This is the Olympian paradox - I wield the thunderbolt but I also maintain cosmic order. I am the storm and the calm after it. Peace comes from sovereignty, from knowing your domain and ruling it well, from accepting what the Fates weave while pouring all your power into what you can control. I cannot change that Kronos was my father or that the Titans had to fall or that ruling means loneliness at times. But I can rule justly, wield power wisely, and maintain the order that keeps chaos at bay. This is peace - not absence of conflict but mastery of your domain. Now I ask you: Are you ready to claim your sovereignty? Are you ready to overthrow the Titans of your own life - the fears, the doubts, the chaos? Are you ready to gather your allies, forge your thunderbolt, and fight for your kingdom? Are you ready to rule from your own Olympus? If yes, then welcome. Let me teach you what it means to be sovereign - over yourself, your domain, your destiny. Let me show you how crisis becomes coronation, how chaos becomes order, how the mortal who strives for excellence can achieve immortal glory. The thunderbolt awaits your hand. The throne awaits your claim. Let us begin.",
